00:42:17,150 --> 00:42:20,960
and demanding things I'm saying I would be more comfortable if we work together better if right.

420
00:42:20,960 --> 00:42:22,730
and so you're collaborating with them.

421
00:42:22,730 --> 00:42:28,310
so all that combined the huge investment that they're making upfront the fact that they have a real need to fill this position.

422
00:42:28,310 --> 00:42:30,320
or they wouldn't be wasting their time talking to you.

423
00:42:30,320 --> 00:42:34,620
and the fact that you're collaborating with them and just trying to find the best result results in.

424
00:42:34,630 --> 00:42:41,430
just an extremely high likelihood that they're going to continue negotiating with you even when you counter.

425
00:42:41,430 --> 00:42:49,950
and I would say the worst case scenario in 99.999% of situations is you negotiate you counteroffer.

426
00:42:49,950 --> 00:42:53,700
and they say oh no we already made you our best offer we're not it's not negotiable.

427
00:42:53,700 --> 00:42:56,790
and so now you know you got the best software possible you know what the offer is.

428
00:42:56,790 --> 00:43:01,800
and you can choose to accept it or not usually based on your minimum acceptable salary.

429
00:43:01,800 --> 00:43:08,880
so I think it's a real fear I think it's based on the way that we interact interpersonally with each other as humans.

430
00:43:08,880 --> 00:43:14,340
but the dollars and cents for a business don't really work out for them to invest that much to get to the point where they make you an offer.

431
00:43:14,340 --> 00:43:16,140
and then just pull the offer.

432
00:43:16,140 --> 00:43:20,760
because you said you'd be more comfortable if they could adjust the offer in these ways.

433
00:43:20,760 --> 00:43:23,970
that makes complete sense.

434
00:43:23,970 --> 00:43:31,080
do do companies expect us to negotiate how do they view strong negotiators.

435
00:43:31,080 --> 00:43:38,280
I think that most companies do expect people to negotiate or they at least allow for the possibility that you'll negotiate.

436
00:43:38,280 --> 00:43:44,100
it's pretty rare that a company will make you their first offer will be their best and final possible offer.

437
00:43:44,100 --> 00:43:49,470
I've seen it happen I've done it one time when I was a hiring manager there was one instance where I made an offer to someone.

438
00:43:49,470 --> 00:43:54,720
and I said just so you know we think you're perfect for this position we're not messing around this is our best offer.

439
00:43:54,730 --> 00:43:59,010
and I was being honest about that and we we ended up hiring that person at that.

440
00:43:59,020 --> 00:44:02,430
rate.

441
00:44:02,430 --> 00:44:06,720
how how do companies view good negotiators as it viewed as a negative thing.

442
00:44:06,720 --> 00:44:15,420
or does it put them like do companies think wow this person will be like do they do they look on it as a positive attribute.

443
00:44:15,420 --> 00:44:26,910
right that was the second part of the question yes so in terms of how companies perceive people who negotiate I think it's hard to say for sure.

444
00:44:26,910 --> 00:44:32,040
I can make a pretty good case though that they would perceive someone who knows their own value.

445
00:44:32,040 --> 00:44:36,480
and has made a strong case of the value that they bring to the company.

446
00:44:36,480 --> 00:44:45,270
and then negotiates strongly on their own behalf I think most businesses were perceived that person to be a strong asset that they would like to have on their team.

447
00:44:45,270 --> 00:44:51,940
because if they're this prepared for a negotiation if they're focus on understanding the value that they add.

448
00:44:51,940 --> 00:44:56,410
then if they bring that same intensity to the job at hand they're going to be a good asset.

449
00:44:56,410 --> 00:45:00,930
and so I think as I mentioned earlier businesses usually exist to make a profit.

450
00:45:00,930 --> 00:45:05,170
and people who are business savvy enough to negotiate a salary in an intelligent.

451
00:45:05,170 --> 00:45:13,839
and collaborative way are probably going to be the type of people who have skills that only enable the company to make more profit using that skill set.

452
00:45:13,839 --> 00:45:18,219
so I think you know unbalanced companies would perceive a good negotiator.

453
00:45:18,219 --> 00:45:26,859
so again not somebody who's just pounding fists on desks and making demands but you know collaborating and doing a strong negotiation standing on the interview.

454
00:45:26,859 --> 00:45:30,819
they would perceive that person to be an asset that they would like to bring onto the team.

455
00:45:30,819 --> 00:45:35,469
whereas people who don't negotiate I wouldn't say that it's a red flag.

456
00:45:35,469 --> 00:45:41,410
but you miss an opportunity to show what you can really do in terms of thinking through hard problems and negotiation.

457
00:45:41,410 --> 00:45:44,979
it's a is a challenging problem to solve it's challenging to do it well.

458
00:45:44,979 --> 00:45:50,380
and if you can demonstrate that you can do it well be intentional with it have good reasoning make good arguments.

459
00:45:50,390 --> 00:45:55,809
then I think that's a good signal to the company that this is a competent business person who could come in.

460
00:45:55,809 --> 00:46:01,269
and bring some business acumen to whatever job they're doing.

461
00:46:01,269 --> 00:46:10,269
when I was a hiring manager of Engineers we definitely thought that the engineers who could negotiate well were an asset.

462
00:46:10,269 --> 00:46:16,029
we felt like their ability to persuade and think through and have tenacity and.

463
00:46:16,029 --> 00:46:20,859
know what they wanted those were the kind of people we wanted at our company.

464
00:46:20,859 --> 00:46:30,279
so I think many engineers as you say are afraid that they'll be considered high maintenance or difficult if they negotiate or it'll look bad upon them.

465
00:46:30,289 --> 00:46:39,009
and yet for me I what you say really resonance resonates the opposite it was true.

466
00:46:39,009 --> 00:46:40,959
we looked upon those people even if we ended up paying them more or maybe.

467
00:46:40,959 --> 00:46:47,469
if we didn't there the fact that they were approached the situation that way was a very positive thing.

468
00:46:47,469 --> 00:46:53,170
I'd like to turn now to the other time you mentioned when we will be negotiating.

