00:46:53,170 --> 00:47:04,730
we've talked a lot about when we join a company that initial offer but once you're in the door and having spent 14 years of an enterprise company.

470
00:47:04,730 --> 00:47:12,200
I spent far more time getting salary increases than I did my initial sort of onboarding.

471
00:47:12,200 --> 00:47:14,600
so I'm curious let's talk about that.

472
00:47:14,610 --> 00:47:23,120
opportunity sometimes annually to negotiate your salary at the evaluation or the raise time.

473
00:47:23,120 --> 00:47:31,370
is there an opportunity to negotiate because that's my first question I don't know that I ever perceived there was.

474
00:47:31,370 --> 00:47:36,800
when I worked at a large company but what is your experience show.

475
00:47:36,800 --> 00:47:44,750
I think you came at this question from exactly the right perspective which is most people are aware that there's an annual opportunity to.

476
00:47:44,750 --> 00:47:47,300
if not discuss compensation to adjust it at most companies.

477
00:47:47,300 --> 00:47:53,000
and the question about whether that's a good time to discuss a raise.

478
00:47:53,000 --> 00:47:58,100
or to negotiate is based on a couple of things but the big one is is there budget available.

479
00:47:58,100 --> 00:48:02,120
and that question will have different answers at different companies.

480
00:48:02,120 --> 00:48:09,890
um first let me take one step back and just say to be clear we're talking about not your standard sort of you've been here another year here's one.

481
00:48:09,890 --> 00:48:12,470
and a half or two percent thanks for being part of our company.

482
00:48:12,470 --> 00:48:19,160
but we're talking about I want a ten percent raise for fifteen members I want a market adjustment I want something to say.

