00:48:46,850 --> 00:48:53,900
or is it done ad hoc or is it based on anniversary date from when people are hired.

488
00:48:53,900 --> 00:49:00,260
so if everyone is going through that process at the same time every year more likely than not there's going to be a fixed budget at the corporate level.

489
00:49:00,270 --> 00:49:06,950
that is then kind of sliced up by let's say business division or Department and then sliced up again by manager.

490
00:49:06,950 --> 00:49:12,890
and so there's not quite fixed but more or less fixed budget that's available.

491
00:49:12,890 --> 00:49:20,790
and so and this is a case where it is of zero sum so in that case if I get a 10% raise and ever the average raises 2%.

492
00:49:20,800 --> 00:49:24,750
either one person is the several people are gonna get nothing.

493
00:49:24,750 --> 00:49:28,230
or a lot of people are gonna get slightly less than 2% to compensate for the wreck.

494
00:49:28,230 --> 00:49:31,770
that I'm the fact that I'm gobbling up some of that budget for my 10%.

495
00:49:31,770 --> 00:49:41,400
so there's the answer is there's really not additional budget or real budget available for you know market adjustments and large raises to negotiate.

496
00:49:41,400 --> 00:49:43,170
so that's not a great time to pursue that on the other hand.

497
00:49:43,170 --> 00:49:48,690
if you're either ad hoc which means some companies are going to the system where it's just sort of you come talk to us.

