00:49:50,640 --> 00:49:54,870
or we'll schedule some time with you if we have a performance review feedback for you.

500
00:49:54,870 --> 00:50:02,970
or if it's anniversary which means you know every year on the anniversary of your start date we're gonna evaluate your performance and talk about salary.

501
00:50:02,970 --> 00:50:11,880
then usually there's not a fixed budget and so you can kind of make your own budget or make your case for your own budget to be allocated.

502
00:50:11,880 --> 00:50:16,109
so it's a little bit more let's say bureaucratic there's more red tape more approvals that need to be done.

503
00:50:16,119 --> 00:50:23,490
but there isn't that sort of fixed budget that you're fighting for a piece of and instead you can kind of make your own budget.

504
00:50:23,490 --> 00:50:27,510
so that's the first levels is their budget how do you know a good rule of thumb is.

505
00:50:27,510 --> 00:50:31,200
if everybody in my company gets raises and promotions at the same time probably not budget there.

506
00:50:31,200 --> 00:50:36,930
so you should go off cycle wait till six months out right in the middle between those two and there may be budget there.

507
00:50:36,930 --> 00:50:43,109
and for everybody else if it's ad-hoc or anniversary based there probably is budget.

508
00:50:43,109 --> 00:50:46,109
so I think that that was more or less your questions when's the good time to do it.

509
00:50:46,109 --> 00:50:50,190
so yes you can negotiate for higher salary you should wait until there's a budget.

