00:53:01,799 --> 00:53:10,470
if you do work someplace without a regularly scheduled time to discuss salary and increases how do you know.

535
00:53:10,470 --> 00:53:18,950
when you should do that and how do you open that conversation because it seems kind of intimidating right.

536
00:53:18,950 --> 00:53:24,150
so this is where my my method is built for this situation that you described.

537
00:53:24,150 --> 00:53:31,319
so when I'm coaching people or you know I teach a class sometimes to kind of walk people through this process.

538
00:53:31,319 --> 00:53:35,940
the taking control of that situation and making a good case for yourself is paramount.

539
00:53:35,940 --> 00:53:41,160
and you may bump into these other constraints but the ability to do that effectively is is what's key.

540
00:53:41,160 --> 00:53:45,200
and the way that you do that is by essentially reverse engineering the raise or promotion that you're pursuing.

541
00:53:45,210 --> 00:53:50,480
so I can kind of talk about both at the same time raises and promotions are in my mind they're separate things.

542
00:53:50,480 --> 00:53:58,490
I wrote them as separate chapters in my book but the process the actual steps that you take to get a raise or a promotion are virtually identical.

543
00:53:58,490 --> 00:54:03,470
and so in both cases where you start is what is it specifically that I'm asking for.

544
00:54:03,470 --> 00:54:09,740
what is the target job that I believe I'm ready to be promoted to what is the target salary that I have in mind.

545
00:54:09,740 --> 00:54:13,160
and of course that target salary would be based on your market value research.

546
00:54:13,160 --> 00:54:18,890
and things like that but the idea is that you want to know specifically what you're asking for.

547
00:54:18,890 --> 00:54:20,650
the main reason for that is you want to make it easy on your manager.

548
00:54:20,650 --> 00:54:23,690
so Marcus you were hiring managers he probably had some of these conversations.

549
00:54:23,700 --> 00:54:29,360
it's much easier to talk about raises and promotions with somebody who comes to you.

550
00:54:29,360 --> 00:54:32,930
and says I would like a raise to this amount or I would like a promotion to this job.

551
00:54:32,930 --> 00:54:36,980
then it needs to talk with somebody who comes to you says I want more money right.

552
00:54:36,980 --> 00:54:44,450
it's it's hard to have that conversation because the first question is well how much more and why those are the two questions that the manager has.

553
00:54:44,450 --> 00:54:49,670
and so your job as an employee who's seeking a RZR promotion is to make that manager's job as easy as possible by setting a very clear goal.

554
00:54:49,680 --> 00:55:00,260
and then before you ever have that conversation making a very good case that you have already demonstrated that you've achieved that goal that you're ready for that goal.

